s, vocals), Elvis did one take where the Jordanaires made a mistake, then a false start, and almost gave up until RCA A&R man Steve Scholes insisted on its potential. The final take still contains a mistake, with someone bumping into a microphone during the spoken bridge, due to the dark recording conditions. It became a massive success and remained in Elvis's repertoire until his last shows. \"Although even the finished take of the song contains one mistake.\"","year":1960,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"A History of Rock Music in 500 Songs","episode":"Episode 82: \"Are You Lonesome Tonight?\" by Elvis Presley","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B0puRvUVwww"}]}],"book_tracks":[],"others":[{"id":138240031229065,"type":"song","name":"Don't Be Cruel","year":1956,"weight":39},{"id":9847353165646,"type":"song","name":"Heartbreak Hotel","year":1956,"weight":32},{"id":105556708779181,"type":"album","name":"Elvis Presley","year":1956,"weight":29},{"id":208627001131508,"type":"song","name":"Hound Dog","year":1956,"weight":27},{"id":76944695519233,"type":"song","name":"It's Now or Never","year":1960,"weight":23},{"id":34702512581755,"type":"song","name":"Jailhouse Rock","year":1957,"weight":22},{"id":276529003025889,"type":"album","name":"From Elvis in Memphis","year":1969,"weight":21},{"id":196759143525117,"type":"song","name":"That's When Your Heartaches Begin","year":1953,"weight":13},{"id":175396590281895,"type":"song","name":"My Happiness","year":2015,"weight":13},{"id":175138481724078,"type":"song","name":"Suspicious Minds","year":1969,"weight":13},{"id":134671177660864,"type":"song","name":"Mystery Train","year":1955,"weight":13},{"id":118494505085544,"type":"song","name":"Trouble","year":1958,"weight":13}]}